    "raw_method_signature": "http_should_keep_alive",
    "codewiki_doc": "Determines if the connection should be kept alive after the current message.",
    "doc_source": "bullet",
    "codewiki_context": "4. Utility Functions",
    "source_file": "overview.md",
    "matched": true,
    "match_score": 1.0,
    "match_strategy": "exact",
    "db_id": "http-parser_http_parser_h_http_should_keep_alive",
    "db_ids": [
      "http-parser_http_parser_c_http_should_keep_alive",
      "http-parser_http_parser_h_http_should_keep_alive"
    ],
    "db_function_name": "http_should_keep_alive",
    "signature": "int http_should_keep_alive(const http_parser * parser)",
    "return_type": "int",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "parser",
        "type": "const http_parser *"
      }
    ],
    "source_code": "int\nhttp_should_keep_alive (const http_parser *parser)\n{\n  if (parser->http_major > 0 && parser->http_minor > 0) {\n    /* HTTP/1.1 */\n    if (parser->flags & F_CONNECTION_CLOSE) {\n      return 0;\n    }\n  } else {\n    /* HTTP/1.0 or earlier */\n    if (!(parser->flags & F_CONNECTION_KEEP_ALIVE)) {\n      return 0;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return !http_message_needs_eof(parser);\n}",
    "cleaned_doc": "If http_should_keep_alive() in the on_headers_complete or\non_message_complete callback returns 0, then this should be\nthe last message on the connection.\nIf you are the server, respond with the \"Connection: close\" header.\nIf you are the client, close the connection."
  },
